{"kind":"event","event_id":4561,"event_uid":"01M2K8BFVG7DW5T6WWKQVMB46T","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":216,"issue_uid":"01M2K7CQVHTA4MBYXR2S136A4X","issue_short_id":"6a4x","actor":"engine:run-152","hlc_physical_ms":1789500178288,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"5ea2646ffe60100ab4118ddd1d5d0e582dd898a57dce3e5c18705ef03a6348f1","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K8BFVG7DW5T6WWKPC88ZP4","author":"engine:run-152","body":"{\"kind\":\"driver:attention\",\"task\":\"1\",\"attention\":\"ok\",\"msg\":\"session ended without hand-off\",\"actor\":\"\",\"id\":\"01M2K8BFTY000083S1DJATN9TM\",\"ts\":1789500178270}","created_at":"2026-09-15T19:22:58.288114557Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T19:22:58.288Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4562,"event_uid":"01M2K8RJQJ7ETRZ2PJSGEKG484","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":216,"issue_uid":"01M2K7CQVHTA4MBYXR2S136A4X","issue_short_id":"6a4x","actor":"impl:1@run-152","hlc_physical_ms":1789500607218,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"40eaca6dfd755ffe354a133424ef1cc462454bbafafa18498c841cc49ecac56e","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K8RJQH93S293B4N2KGPZ65","author":"impl:1@run-152","body":"Anchors: the three-way is bought in the SNAPSHOT, not in the fold.\n\nThe obvious implementation — re-root the frontier mid-fold, `files[p] = update_state(anchor_base.files[p], current_lines(files[p]))` just before `merge_states` — passes every single-anchor case and breaks a mixed wave. Two tasks anchored at BASE plus one anchored at the wave's own `--base` (H1) lost ALL THREE edits and narrated a spurious conflict: the re-root rewrites the frontier so it descends from the anchor, while a later base-anchored task's weave still descends from the base snapshot, so the two share no ancestry and `merge_states` reads disjoint edits as a conflict. It is also order-dependent, which the K1 self-check would have caught as exit 3 — except the conflict path returns before self-checks run.\n\nWhat shipped instead (`rw.chained_snapshots` + `ff.anchored_inputs`): the wave's base and every anchor it carries are read as ONE chain. Per path, the oldest tree carrying it is the root (`initial_state`); each later anchor is `update_state` of its predecessor; the base is `update_state` of the last anchor. A task publishes over its own anchor's link in that chain. Every weave in the wave then has one root, `merge_states` is unchanged (so still commutative), and the anchored merge is the three-way over the anchor by construction.\n\nVerified: the mixed wave folds clean in all three task orders with the same candidate and `selfChecks: ok`; the M2 transcript is byte-identical to the BASE kernel (same candidate tree, no `anchor` key) both without `@` and with `@<base>`; 263 passed.\n\nAside, not a defect: two tasks editing ADJACENT lines narrate one conflict. The BASE kernel does this too with no anchors involved — it is the vendored kernel's region granularity, not something anchors introduced.","created_at":"2026-09-15T19:30:07.217769306Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T19:30:07.218Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4563,"event_uid":"01M2K956WRDQGAZ0Q9D1S6JEPF","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.metadata_updated","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":216,"issue_uid":"01M2K7CQVHTA4MBYXR2S136A4X","issue_short_id":"6a4x","actor":"impl:1@run-152","hlc_physical_ms":1789501021080,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"752124070d0b6e51367ab6037e48dcd1ae2f857c5db8acb2c089e99978d91059","payload":{"diff":{"work.attention_msg":{"from":"session ended without hand-off","to":"Anchored patch folding shipped: --patch <id>=<file>@<anchorSha> on fold/resolve/materialize, anchor recorded on the fold event, three-way over the anchor. 263 passed; M2 byte-identical to the BASE kernel; vendor and the frozen fleet paths untouched."}},"revision_new":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-15T19:37:01.080Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T19:37:01.08Z"}
